From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:33:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: add video to 1:1 Signal calls

The media engine (signal-call-media) can now send and receive VP8
video, so the Phone app can be given a video call.

- A video call is placed with Offer type OFFER_VIDEO_CALL when the
  dialer asks for one ("video": true). An incoming video Offer rings
  as a video call (incomingVideoState "available").
- changeMedia turns our camera on or off. It sends VIDEO to the
  engine, which sends no video before the call is answered and tells
  the far side in RingRTC's SenderStatus. An outgoing call gives the
  engine its call id (CALLID) for that message. incomingVideo hides
  or shows the far side's picture.
- The engine's video lines are passed to call.c (call_video.rs parses
  them; call_video.c keeps the state):
  - VSHM: the decoded picture's gst-shm socket, the payload's
    videoURI.
  - VPREVIEW: the self-view.
  - VTX: outgoingVideo.
  - PEERVIDEO: incomingVideo and "streaming".
  - PEERROT: incomingVideoOrientation.
  - VIDEOERR: logged.
- audiod is told "video": true for a call with video, again when a
  voice call turns into one.

call_video.rs and call_video.c have their own tests (rustc --test;
src/c/tests/test_call_video.c with glib only).

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
